<title>LEBANON: Only six-month T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</title>
<headline>Only six-month T-bill yields fall in Beirut.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields on six-month Lebanese treasury bills for the May 1 issue fell while rates on the remaining categories held steady.</p>
<p>The bank issued the following rate details (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				 percent)		    (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	   13.25 (13.26)		13.70 (13.70)</p>
<p>    Six months	     13.48 (13.48)		14.44 (14.45)</p>
<p>    12 month		 13.20 (13.20)		15.20 (15.20)</p>
<p>    24 month   (interest payable twice early)     16.08 (16.08)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (9611) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
